{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And they said, each man… 'It is man…'</b> One needs to know what the verse's intention is in this. Perhaps it is that when they saw it, HaShem prepared it for their mouths in place of what they said — 'What is it?' — so they said 'It is man,' and this is its name which HaShem fixed and placed the name in Israel's mouth, in the manner of the Sages of blessed memory's statement (Berakhot 7b): 'who placed names in the earth' — meaning the names the Creator called them. And the verse's saying <b>for they did not know</b> gives the reason for the name's arrival on their lips: it is because they did not know what it was, and from that very uncertainty it fell to them in their mouths. Or perhaps from this Israel showed cleverness and called its name 'man,' as it is written (Exodus 16:31): 'and the house of Israel called its name man' — for they discerned in the word 'man' something not usual in the wilderness, and this can only be the spirit of HaShem speaking, His word upon their tongue, for this is its name."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:50.296141444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}